<title>USA: Primark unit settles harassment, bias case.</title>
<headline>Primark unit settles harassment, bias case.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triad International Maintenance Co., or Timco, will pay $140,000 to settle charges that it allowed racial discrimination and sexual harassment at its North Carolina facilities, the Washington Post reported.</p>
<p>Timco is a unit of Primark Corp.</p>
<p>Under the terms of Timco's settlement with the U.S. Labor Department, the company will offer at least seven employees back pay and reinstatement or compensation for fringe benefits and salary increases they would have received if they had been promoted, the newspaper said, quoting a Timco official.</p>
</text>
